tract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [tester] tester (codex) (run=RUN-260730-3716a5, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [tester] tester (codex) (run=RUN-260730-3716a5)\nTESTER DIAGNOSIS 2026-07-30 cycle 5: Native ssh win probe reproduced the worker failure before Go. The inherited launch pipe was present at handle 528 with the exact 88-byte csk-go-launch-v1 record, but the manager PID was 13192 while the executing worker PID 2136 reported parent PID 2780. Windows venv Scripts/python.exe is a redirector process, so _parse_worker_launch_record rejects direct-child ownership; cli.main then falls through to argparse (exit 2, invalid hidden choice), and the manager later receives BrokenPipeError at _write_message. Minimal defensible fix is the candidate already appearing in the producer worktree: on Windows launch the identity-bound runtime.base_executable.path, keep the installed csk.exe as the fixed script/mode, and accept/prove that bound base process image. Required regression: synthetic Windows venv identity asserts worker_argv selects base_executable, plus native Windows capability/fixture proof that hidden dispatch remains alive and accepted builds pass. Diagnostic scripts/logs will be attached in the tester outcome; no product source edited.\nTESTER FOLLOW-UP 2026-07-30: Producer candidate closes the venv redirector ancestry defect, but native rerun still has 3 accepted-case failures: worker now returns build_execution_worker_identity_invalid installed manager launcher is unavailable. Native console-archive overlay proves distlib rewrites sys.argv[0] from ...\Scripts\csk.exe to the nonexistent extensionless ...\Scripts\csk before csk.cli.main, while sys.orig_argv remains exactly [base python.exe, -S, -s, -B, -P, installed csk.exe, __csk-go-worker-v1]. Therefore run_worker defaults worker_executable to a nonexistent path. Minimal closed fix: after consuming the authenticated launch capability, derive/pass worker_executable from the one validated fixed sys.orig_argv launcher slot (or an equally closed fixed-argv helper), then let expected manager identity matching reject any discrepancy; do not use extensionless sys.argv[0]. Required unit negative/positive: fixed orig argv selects csk.exe; malformed, extra, reordered, programmatic, or non-capability argv never dispatches. Required native rerun: all accepted Windows fixture cases. Diagnostic command exit 0; no product source edited.\nTESTER CYCLE-5 CLOSURE 2026-07-30: After the redirector and distlib launcher fixes, native candidate4 exposed an unavoidable Windows Python-home sys.path entry. Allowing it unbound would admit root-level code before proof, so the defensible fix binds the complete bounded python_home import tree while excluding site-package trees disabled by -S/-s. Tester regression first exited 1 with 2 failures: stale startup-root deserialization and omitted existing python314.zip; after exact _manager_runtime_roots validation and fixed-slot archive binding it exited 0 with 2 passed. Unchanged candidate6 Windows fixture exited 0: 5 passed/5 host skips, all 3 accepted variants plus hidden-literal/runtime-image negatives. Independent tester plain accepted fixture exited 0: 1 passed/no skips in 63.33s. Local focused pytest 118 passed/1 skip, strict mypy 65 files, compileall, and tabnanny all exited 0. Whole-module unit branch coverage measured 54%, so the 80% whole-file checklist item remains unchecked. Evidence and exact commands are in TASK-260720-2g21eg_tester-windows-worker-diagnosis.md and attached JUnit outcomes.\nTESTER EXACT-CANDIDATE ADDENDUM 2026-07-30: Candidate 8 wheel SHA-256 8cc70ef4ef574088c0c017905b6a5609820a6f2bdc3e984b6b1669674ba9af4f contains go_v1.py SHA-256 abdf349c3ff2ebad7f17c25480655e65134378b1a402c7de9e010de3a684fcd4, byte-equal to handoff source. Native macOS fixture exit 0: 10 passed/no skips, JUnit 63.985s. Native Windows exact-wheel fixture exit 0: 5 passed/5 host skips, JUnit 287.548s. Independent tester Window