ent) with nothing load-bearing dropped. Windows test-assumption changes verified against product code (_manager_runtime_roots, _manager_windows_stdlib_root, _runtime_archive_slots). Independent gates (all exit 0 unless noted): macOS focused 141 passed; forced-Linux focused 129 passed/12 skipped; NATIVE Windows focused 131 passed/10 skipped over ssh with all four payload SHA-256 confirmed equal remotely and test+skip sets identical to the developer XML, closing the standing native-Windows caveat from cycles 5-6; macOS full 1159/21; Windows full 1063 passed/116 skipped with one environmental PowerShell ExecutionPolicy failure in test_shell_init.py (zero go_v1 references; passes 8/14 with RemoteSigned), equivalent to the claimed 1064/116; configured strict mypy and mypy --platform linux both 0 issues/65 files; wheel build + fresh-venv install byte-identical; native macOS Go 1.25.5 real fixture 10 passed; hygiene clean. All seven attached cycle-6 artifacts hash exactly to the handoff table. Handoff pinned conformance commit f5d7673 is not an ancestor of the accepted root 0aae5df, but both carry the identical conformance/v1 tree 0ea6b716..., so no vector staleness. NON-BLOCKING FINDING: fixed_environment is asserted against a hand transcription, not the vector -- test_worker_environment_matches_the_fixed_darwin_vector compares one test literal to another and no test in the repo references fixed_environment, making it the only AC-named vector element not pinned by test_accepted_rc5_vectors_match_the_implementation. I verified the transcription equals the accepted vector 28/28 keys and values, so there is no correctness defect today; construction lives in toolchain.py (TASK-260720-3j8pp5) while this task correctly enforces the environment via _validate_worker_environment. Residual risk is silent drift on a future rc; fix is to compare against drivers[fixed_environment] in the existing vector test. Recommend a follow-up, not a seventh cycle. Cycle-5 verdict wording that thi