re native Darwin `RENAME_EXCL` / Linux `RENAME_NOREPLACE` selection. Identical concurrent winners are reused byte-for-byte; different bytes produce a stable conflict. Untrusted or corrupt candidates are quarantined under the caller-held guard and never adopted.\n- DARWIN FINDING: Darwin rejects directory rename when the source directory lacks owner write permission, including sealed `0500` state. Locked quarantine now reserves a unique target, grants owner control only through verified no-follow state, atomically moves the candidate, and restores its prior mode in quarantine; `0700`, `0550`, `0000`, and sealed `0500` cases pass.\n- GATES: POSIX-focused pytest exited 0 with 33 passed; full accepted-root pytest exited 0 with 882 passed / 6 skipped; strict mypy exited 0 over 63 source files; compileall, diff hygiene, distribution build, and Twine metadata each exited 0. The repository declares no separate style linter.\n- EVIDENCE: board outcome `TASK-260720-2jfnz6_implementation-evidence.md`; no Windows ACL, installer transaction, status, or GC behavior is claimed.\n\n### 2026-07-30 — Fixed go-v1 compile-driver cycle-2 review finds an open startup TCB\n- REVIEWER: `TASK-260720-2g21eg` on the unchanged CocoaSkills candidate rooted at `97a0ed870782b48eebc5a9c25a9cfa8fea5ff245`; no product source or test file was modified.\n- WORKER TCB FINDING: cycle 2 binds the launcher, interpreter binary/link chain, and installed `site-packages/csk` tree, but launches the ordinary Python console script with `site` startup enabled. A fresh wheel-installed venv accepted a real native Go build while an executable sibling `.pth` hook ran before `csk.cli`; mutating that hook did not change the manager identity digest. The worker's complete mutable startup TCB is therefore still not identity-bound.\n- NATIVE-PROBE FINDING: macOS inventory entries statically marked unavailable bypass `_native_probe`; only 3 of 5 controls were genuinely probed, while all five evidence entries claimed `probed_at=pre-worker-launch`. The rc.5 per-operation rule excludes a host label or build-time constant from being an availability probe.\n- GATE ANOMALY: the authoritative focused run failed 1 of 178 cases because `manager-package-replaced-after-launch` returned `build_execution_control_unavailable` instead of `build_execution_worker_identity_invalid`; the case then passed 10 isolated runs and the full suite passed 861 / skipped 6, demonstrating an order-sensitive or nondeterministic diagnostic boundary. Strict mypy and hygiene remained green.\n- VERDICT: changes requested; route `to-dev`. Evidence and required rework are recorded in `TASK-260720-2g21eg_review-verdict-cycle-2.md`.\n\n### 2026-07-30 — Protected POSIX cache Linux quarantine CI rework\n- TRIGGER: CocoaSkills PR #11 CI run `30514706010` passed strict mypy plus every macOS and Windows test job, but all four Ubuntu versions failed the same four cache tests at `_move_aside` with `PermissionError: [Errno 13]`.\n- ROOT CAUSE: the verified temporary owner-unlock path was gated to Darwin. Linux therefore attempted ordinary quarantine rename with sealed directory modes `0500`, `0550`, or `0000`; owner write/execute control was absent at the rename boundary.\n- FIX: the existing rooted, no-follow, effective-UID and inode-verified unlock now applies to owned POSIX directories generally, skips mutation only when full owner `rwx` is already present, and restores the exact original mode after both successful and failed rename.\n- REGRESSION: Linux-semantic seams force `EACCES` unless the candidate has temporary owner control, cover sealed `0500`, untrusted `0550`, and inaccessible `0000`, and prove exact mode restoration plus reservation cleanup when rename itself fails.\n- GATES: the test-first reproducer exited 1 as expected; final POSIX-focused pytest exited 0 with 37 passed; full accepted-root pytest exited 0 with 886 passed / 6 skipped; strict mypy passed 63 source files; diff hygiene, compileall, distribution build, and Twine metadata all exited 0.\n- EVIDENCE: board outcome `TASK-260720-2jfnz6_linux-ci-rework.md`; the task branch remains unstaged/uncommitted for the commit-owning mover and requires a fresh Ubuntu matrix after integration.\n\n### 2026-07-30 — Fixed go-v1 compile-driver cycle-3 review finds unbound runtime code and a user-selectable hidden mode\n- REVIEWER: `TASK-260720-2g21eg` cycle 3 on CocoaSkills base `495ad021847529ce5a544dba415ca2fe19949539`; clean local `main`, `main`, and `origin/main` matched, both dependency tasks were accepted, and the four candidate hashes matched the producer packet. No CocoaSkills source or test file was modified.\n- RUNTIME-TCB FINDING: the cycle-3 startup identity hashes selected immediate startup hooks and records only the standard-library root inode/mode. Ordinary importable standard-library files are neither identity entries nor retained watch paths, while `validate_worker_runtime` accepts any loaded module path below that root without a content identity. An isolated probe changed the bytes of the worker-imported `json/__init__.py`; manager/startup identity remained equal, the macOS mutation guard closed without an event, and both pre/post runtime proofs were accepted. Mutable Python code can therefore execute before the ready proof without `build_execution_worker_identity_invalid`, leaving the mandatory worker identity and pre/post re-verification boundary open.\n- HIDDEN-MODE FINDING: `cli.main()` checks actual `sys.argv` for `__csk-go-worker-v1` before the public parser. Invoking the installed entry point directly as `csk __csk-go-worker-v1 </dev/null` selected `run_worker`, returned its length-framed worker-protocol failure, and exited 3. The test rejects only programmatic `cli.main([mode])` while explicitly accepting the actual external-CLI path, contrary to the rc.5 requirement that the hidden mode is not a user-visible command surface and no user option selects it.\n- GREEN GATES: accepted-root focused pytest passed 289 / skipped 4; full pytest passed 962 / skipped 6; the separate wheel-installed native macOS Go fixture passed all 6 scenarios; strict mypy passed 62 source files; tabnanny, trailing-whitespace, and diff hygiene passed. Green regression gates do not cover either reproduced boundary.\n- VERDICT: changes requested; route `to-dev`. Evidence and exact rework requirements are in `TASK-260720-2g21eg_review-verdict-cycle-3.md` plus the attached standard-library and hidden-mode probes.\n\n### 2026-07-30 — Protocol v6 rc.6 integrated conformance re-verification\n- DEVELOPER: `TASK-260720-3ag6pi` review cycle 3 continued the exact curator-spec product state at `.temp/TASK-260720-3ag6pi/rework-cycle-3`, based on published rc.5 `f5d7673039226ab81de2f4f87e2155ae995c4df3`. A byte-identical unsigned, untagged, task-local clean checkout at `ddb181ca3b8e243f212e90ff26fcabe2234fb669` was used only for release-gate validation.\n- REGRESSION CLOSED: all 22 accepted compiled lifecycle cases and their fail-closed validator/release guards are restored on the current `manager-worker-v1` cache and receipt identities. After normalizing only execution-policy/cache-key/receipt identity changes, the current lifecycle vector is byte-identical to accepted `TASK-260720-cw39jh`, normalized SHA-256 `11fe66182e719e8e5c067d3ff2ab646dd889de7c97130881fcacdbf9694a7b6c`.\n- GATES: `make validate`, two independent regenerations, recursive byte comparison, `make regenerate-check`, and `make release-check VERSION=1.0.0-rc.6` all exited 0. Validation covered 42 schemas, 447 manifest entries, 59 Python tests, and Go tests with no skips. Both regeneration aggregates were `8255898b37dd1f3b95423804bd0c35bd7ec48a16fbbe9b4d9e4cecc830900072`. The literal superseded rc.4 release command truthfully exited 2.\n- COMPATIBILITY: agent-skill/csk-skill schemas 1–5, install-marker-v1, claim-v1, and 24 baseline cases are byte-identical to rc.5 `origin/main` and pre-v6 baseline `57c1f568…`; rc.5 release metadata remains byte-frozen at SHA-256 `75ae17fc029b4f51ca40ce768d04fd72991ec3db2602b8fe59213bee6ac34583`.\n- SAFETY: all 77 build-driver rejections require no artifact execution or reuse; rc.6 emits no claim, advances no committed downstream pin, and claims no hardened profile. No authoritative commit, push, tag, release, checksum, signature, attestation, or implementation pin was created.\n- EVIDENCE: new cycle-3 raw logs, manifest/legacy/lifecycle/safety audits, acceptance/rejection matrix, and outcome report are attached to the board under `TASK-260720-3ag6pi_cycle-3-*`.\n\n### 2026-07-30 — Protected POSIX cache mode-0000 capability rework closes Linux review\n- DEVELOPER REWORK: `TASK-260720-2jfnz6` retained the published CocoaSkills task branch at HEAD `0d6ad16fce35c1bd8854511e13766cd236908e3b` and base `495ad021847529ce5a544dba415ca2fe19949539`. The final unstaged product delta contains only `cache_posix.py` and its focused tests; `cache.py` matches HEAD and no `uv.lock` remains.\n- CAPABILITY: inaccessible owned Linux directories are acquired through rooted `O_PATH | O_NOFOLLOW | O_DIRECTORY` references and changed with `fchmodat2(AT_EMPTY_PATH)`. Unsupported kernels or architectures fail closed with `cache_protection_unsupported`; no path-following chmod fallback is adopted.\n- FAILURE SAFETY: unlock now occurs before destination reservation. Original mode is restored and reservations are removed across fsync, reopen, rename, retry, unsupported-capability, and cleanup failures. Tests cover sealed `0500`, untrusted `0550`, inaccessible `0000`, exact restoration, and zero reservation leakage.\n- NATIVE MATRIX: a disposable Ubuntu 26.04 Linux 7.0/aarch64 Lima VM ran the exact focused suite with pytest 9.1.1 on Python 3.11.15, 3.12.13, 3.13.12, and 3.14.3. Each standalone gate exited 0 with 40 passed and no skips. The VM was stopped and deleted after evidence capture; Homebrew Lima 2.2.0 remains installed.\n- HOST GATES: exact post-scope macOS focused pytest exited 0 with 39 passed