idence and updated all-pass story/rejection matrix are attached as `TASK-260720-3ag6pi_cycle-4-*`.\n\n### 2026-07-30 — Protected POSIX cache identity-stable publication closes R3 race\n- DEVELOPER REWORK: `TASK-260720-2jfnz6` retained the CocoaSkills task branch at HEAD `0d6ad16fce35c1bd8854511e13766cd236908e3b` and base `495ad021847529ce5a544dba415ca2fe19949539`. The unstaged product delta remains exactly `cache_posix.py` and its focused tests; `cache.py` matches HEAD.\n- RACE CLOSED: publication now retains the rooted no-follow staged-directory descriptor across atomic rename and seals only that exact inode. If another publisher moves it during the private-mode seal window, the first publisher never seals or quarantines the replacement by logical name; it opens the selected live winner read-only and compares pinned canonical receipt and artifact bytes.\n- DETERMINISTIC PROOF: publisher A is paused after rename until publisher B exceeds the retry window, quarantines A, publishes and seals a different inode, and returns. Identical bytes yield B=`published`, A=`reused-winner`; different bytes yield B=`published`, A=`CacheConflictError`. Both schedules leave a protected live hit, a sealed quarantined loser, and empty staging.\n- NATIVE MATRIX: exact mounted hashes passed the full POSIX cache file on disposable Ubuntu 26.04 / Linux 7.0 / aarch64 with CPython 3.11.15, 3.12.13, 3.13.14, and 3.14.6; each standalone gate exited 0 with 42 passed and no skips. The VM was stopped and deleted.\n- HOST GATES: focused pytest exited 0 with 41 passed / 1 Linux-only skip; full accepted-root pytest exited 0 with 890 passed / 7 skipped; strict mypy passed 63 source files; task-scoped Ruff, compileall, diff hygiene, distribution build, and Twine metadata all exited 0.\n- EVIDENCE: board outcome `TASK-260720-2jfnz6_r3-identity-stable-publication-evidence.md` records exact commands, exit codes, candidate hashes, non-green setup diagnostics, and VM cleanup.\n\n### 2026-07-30 — Fixed go-v