rk must bind the actual interpreter runtime/load components through every identity phase, resolve Windows base-runtime semantics securely, and add native runtime-mutation and Windows wheel-in-venv coverage. Evidence: `TASK-260720-2g21eg_review-verdict-cycle-4.md` and its task-scoped JUnit outcomes.\n\n### 2026-07-30 — Install transaction engine review finds a macOS canonicalization stampede\n- REVIEWER: `TASK-260720-z2z795` run `RUN-260730-0c7fda` reviewed signed CocoaSkills HEAD `a5ec015c0b5b51149c81a679ce259920a3523374` plus the single unstaged Windows-test delta. No CocoaSkills source or test file was modified by the reviewer.\n- GREEN SCOPE: the repaired Windows permission regressions passed natively and under a forced one-bit Windows identity; a negative control proved both tests detect disabled foreign-mode rejection. The prior 14 lock-integrity regressions, 13 contract cases, focused 129-test suite, strict mypy 2.1/2.3, Ruff, and package build passed.\n- CONCURRENCY FINDING: full Python 3.14 pytest failed `test_repeated_concurrent_home_consumers_survive_release_handoffs` (`1 failed, 807 passed, 58 skipped`), and fresh-process stress reproduced it on iteration 4. A six-second faulthandler dump showed same-home consumer threads still rescanning directory entries in `_canonicalize_darwin_existing_path` before `_ExclusiveFileLock.__enter__` starts its configured timeout.\n- VERDICT: changes requested; route `to-dev`. Rework must bound or eliminate the same-home macOS canonicalization stampede, cover preparation in the acquisition deadline or otherwise bound total acquisition, and add deterministic preparation-interleaving coverage. Evidence: `TASK-260720-z2z795_review-verdict_RUN-260730-0c7fda.md`, validation ledger, and raw-log archive.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
