.task-board/.resources/STORY-260720-1uv5gi/STORY-260720-1uv5gi_spawn-log_-analyst--solution-architect--codex-.log:10844:scope:Work in the csk repository after the csk shared-vector and real-Go end-to-end handoffs plus TASK-260720-2g7avf. Own the compiled-build additions to tests/test_protocol_conformance.py and narrowly related test-only helpers, using CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT. Exercise real manifest parsing, install planning, build and cache behavior, shim launch, argument and exit propagation, and rejection ordering in isolated temporary homes and projects. Extend the existing rc.4 vector consumer rather than replacing it. Do not call or import Curator, copy shared vectors into the repository, weaken no-skip behavior, or change the curator-spec CI pin in this task.
.task-board/.resources/STORY-260720-1uv5gi/STORY-260720-1uv5gi_spawn-log_-analyst--solution-architect--codex-.log:10845:ac:With CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT set, the Python consumer parametrizes every shared compiled-build case exactly once and fails on unknown, missing, duplicate, xfailed, or skipped case IDs. The positive fixture installs from the unmodified suite, excludes build roots from context and runtime copies, builds on a miss, reuses a verified cache entry, performs a compiler-free and mutation-free dry-run including audit-registry state, and launches the installed command with the exact shared stdout, stderr, forwarded arguments, and exit status. Every shared negative case is rejected in the expected normalized class and at the required before-build or before-mutation boundary. Test homes, project roots, Go caches, and subprocess recording are isolated per case; no implementation-owned expected outcome or binary hash is introduced. The focused external-suite tests, full pytest suite, and strict type check pass when the suite is supplied, while developer runs may skip only when the environment variable is absent.
